# Channel pays for Emrakul with life (the operator, 2026-10-21): "the card "Channel" my opponent
# played it, then tried to play emrakul but couldn't." Ruling: "have channel work like phyrexian
# mana".
#
# Seat 0 (human) holds Channel ({G}{G}) and Emrakul, the Aeons Torn ({15}) with two Forests out.
# The Forests pay for Channel; Emrakul is then paid with 15 life through Channel's effect, which
# sits in the Command zone with no card on the table to click.
